 Thom Browne, to seductive elegance with TOM FORD FASHION. The Ermenegildo Zegna Group is internationally recognized for its unique Filiera, owned and controlled by the Group, which is made up of the finest Italian textile producers fully integrated with unique luxury manufacturing capabilities, to ensure superior excellence, quality and innovation capacity. The Ermenegildo Zegna Group has more than 7,200 employees and recorded revenues of €1.92 billion in 2025.","context":"About Ermenegildo Zegna Group","section":"Results of Operations","block":83,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001877787-26-000035","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-03","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001877787","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1877787/000187778726000035/eznv-h12026resultspressrel.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/b26de1bef7af2085352c5ace27a8b94f19dd4daaf64105514456ac05f896361f.bin","sha256":"b26de1bef7af2085352c5ace27a8b94f19dd4daaf64105514456ac05f896361f"}}],"omittedEvidenceCount":0},"managementExplanations":{"status":"evidence_available","evidence":[{"id":"a35422a58299b9e3c4f45de8332a50f65c14393ece84c604fd7754f8ecde452c","quote":"•Adjusted EBIT of €74.5 million, increasing from €68.7 million in H1 2025, with an Adjusted EBIT Margin of 7.5% (7.4% in H1 2025), driven by Zegna segment Adjusted EBIT Margin, up 50bps to 14.8%.","context":"•Profit of €28.4 million (2.9% profit margin), compared to €47.9 million in H1 2025 which included €27.8 million of non-cash gains from the fair value remeasurement of non-controlling interest put option liabilities.","section":"","block":5,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001877787-26-000035","form":"6-K","filedAt":"2026-09-03","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001877787","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1877787/000187778726000035/eznv-h12026